  "examples": [
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲩⲱ ⲁⲛⲣⲱⲙⲉ ⲣⲁⲡⲟⲡⲛⲓⲅⲉ ϩⲓⲧⲙⲡⲉ**ⲥⲧⲟⲓ** ⲙⲡⲗⲓⲃⲁⲛⲟⲥ · ⲙⲛⲡϣⲟⲩϩⲏⲛⲉ ⲉⲧⲉⲣⲉⲛⲣⲱⲙⲉ ⲧⲁⲗⲟ ⲙⲙⲟϥ ⲉϩⲣⲁⲓ : —",
      "english": "and men died, being choked by the fumes of the frankincense^ and by the smell of the incense which the people were offering up upon the altar",
      "source": "Martyrdom of Victor part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:martyrdoms.victor.budge:1-6",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲗⲗⲁ ⲡϣⲱⲗⲙ ⲟⲛ ⲉϥϣⲁⲛϩⲩⲇⲁⲛⲉ ⲛⲥⲁⲡⲉ**ⲥⲧⲟⲓ** ⲉⲧⲛⲁⲛⲟⲩϥ ⲛⲛⲥⲟϭⲛ ⲙⲛⲛϣⲟⲩϩⲏⲛⲉ ϣⲁϥϣⲱⲡⲉ ϩⲛⲟⲩⲁⲡⲁⲧⲏ ·",
      "english": "Yet again in the case of the smell. If the nose be in the habit of taking delight in the things which have sweet smells, that is, in scented unguents, and in aromatic perfumes, and in balsams, it falleth at length into a state of numbness,",
      "source": "On Susanna",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pschrysostom.susanna.budge:1-63",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲡⲉϫⲉⲭⲉⲓⲣⲟⲩⲃⲉⲓⲛ ⲛⲁⲓ ϫⲉϫⲓⲛⲛⲧⲁⲡⲇⲓⲁⲃⲟⲗⲟⲥ ⲃⲱⲕ ⲉϩⲟⲩⲛ ⲉⲡⲡⲁⲣⲁⲇⲓⲥⲟⲥ ⲁϥⲣϩⲁⲗ ⲛⲁⲇⲁⲙ ⲙⲛⲉⲩϩⲁ ⲧⲉϥⲥϩⲓⲙⲉ ⲁⲛϣⲏⲛ ϣⲱⲗⲙ ⲙⲡⲉⲩ**ⲥⲧⲟⲓ** ⲁⲛⲉⲩϭⲱⲱⲃⲉ ϩⲉ ⲉⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ",
      "english": "And the Cherubim said unto me, 'From the moment when the Devil entered into Paradise, and seduced Adam, and Eve his wife, the trees, which up to that time had possessed a sweet smell, ceased to have any smell at all, and their leaves [began to] fall off.",
      "source": "Mysteries of John the Evangelist part 2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:misc.mysteries_john.budge:13-28",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    }
